{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba WORDING-V2.md | sed -n '64,180p'; nl -ba ../../../poc/config/poc-v120.json; nl -ba ../2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/DESIGN.md | sed -n '1,48p'; rg -n 'D705|380 passed' ../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md WORDING-V2.md; rg --files ../.. | rg 'mutants.log|v120-replay' \"","aggregated_output":"    64\trequests grow by about 120 tokens a pair). The completeness check, equality with old-2 and the paid-transport record apply as in the\n    65\tcensus; `draw.json` records the wording.\n    66\t\n    67\t## 5. The product version (D705: version 2 as a separately versioned, reviewed configuration)\n    68\t\n    69\t- **Config:** the matching setting gains `link_questions` (`config.Setting.link_questions`; allowed `links-v1`, `links-v2`), accepted\n    70\t  only with the engine `jev-links` (any other engine naming it is refused) and defaulting to `links-v1` there, so `poc-v119.json` is\n    71\t  unchanged in bytes, checksum and requests. `poc/config/poc-v120.json` = poc-v119 with `\"link_questions\": \"links-v2\"`.\n    72\t- **Code:** `links.py` holds both question sets as literal texts (`READS`, `SIGN` for links-v1; `READS_V2`, `SIGN_V2` for links-v2,\n    73\t  byte-equal to the probe's `window_test.wording_v2()`); `reads_question` and `sign_question` take the version; `choose`, `_signed` and\n    74\t  `_corrected` pass `cfg.matching.link_questions`. Nothing else reads the field.\n    75\t- **Entry points:** unchanged: the ordinary launchers refuse the engine `jev-links` under any question version (D694 §0); poc-v120 runs\n    76\t  only in the measurement harness.\n    77\t\n    78\t| Table | Rows |\n    79\t|---|---|\n    80\t| Value × reader | `Setting.link_questions`: read by `links.choose`, `_signed`, `_corrected` only (searched: no other reader); `model.build_request` and every other step ignore it. The two text sets: read by the two builders only. |\n    81\t| New path × old checks | poc-v119's link requests byte-equal (the v1 pin `LINK_QUESTIONS_SHA` unchanged; `poc-v119.json` untouched); the v2 texts pinned (`LINK_QUESTIONS_V2_SHA`) and equal to the probe's; poc-v120 over the whole window with the probe's own answers replayed by request hash meets every link job of the probe (READS and SIGN) and ends equal to old-2 (`window_test.py v120-replay`); config refuses an unknown question version and the field on another engine. |\n    82\t| State × event | a run keeps one configuration (as for v118/v119, DESIGN.md §0); a store written under poc-v120 and opened under poc-v119 or poc-v118 is read the same (the written rows do not carry the question version; the selection record carries the config checksum); a configuration changed between days is the defined outcome of D694 §0, not a supported mode. |\n    83\t| Prior decisions | D359 (a configuration naming a version the code does not build is refused), D694 §0 (entry points), D695, D703, D705. |\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"version\": \"poc-v120\",\n     3\t  \"_note\": \"poc-v119 with version 2 of the link questions (D703, D705; docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md): a tie-break by the stronger full-period anchor, links across periods only when the supplied text states how, a base-effect example of the opposite sign; runs only in the whole-window measurement harness in this version.\",\n     4\t  \"provider\": \"openai\",\n     5\t  \"search_top_n\": 10,\n     6\t  \"extraction\": {\n     7\t    \"T1\": {\n     8\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n     9\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T1-v74i\",\n    10\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    11\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    12\t    },\n    13\t    \"T2\": {\n    14\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    15\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T2-v74i\",\n    16\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    17\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    18\t    },\n    19\t    \"T3\": {\n    20\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    21\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T3-v74i\",\n    22\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    23\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    24\t    },\n    25\t    \"T4\": {\n    26\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    27\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T4-v74i\",\n    28\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    29\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    30\t    },\n    31\t    \"T5\": {\n    32\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    33\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T5-v74i\",\n    34\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    35\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    36\t    },\n    37\t    \"T6\": {\n    38\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    39\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T6-v74i\",\n    40\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    41\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    42\t    },\n    43\t    \"T7\": {\n    44\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    45\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T7-v74i\",\n    46\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    47\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    48\t    },\n    49\t    \"T8\": {\n    50\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    51\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T8-v74i\",\n    52\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    53\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    54\t    },\n    55\t    \"T10\": {\n    56\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    57\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T10-v74i\",\n    58\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    59\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    60\t    },\n    61\t    \"T11\": {\n    62\t      \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    63\t      \"prompt_version\": \"T11-v74i\",\n    64\t      \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    65\t      \"max_output_tokens\": 12000\n    66\t    }\n    67\t  },\n    68\t  \"matching\": {\n    69\t    \"model\": \"jev-1.14.0\",\n    70\t    \"prompt_version\": \"matching-v3\",\n    71\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    72\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 12000,\n    73\t    \"engine\": \"jev-links\",\n    74\t    \"link_questions\": \"links-v2\"\n    75\t  },\n    76\t  \"rejudging\": {\n    77\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    78\t    \"prompt_version\": \"judging-v8\",\n    79\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    80\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 16000\n    81\t  },\n    82\t  \"final_verdict\": {\n    83\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    84\t    \"prompt_version\": \"verdict-v0\",\n    85\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"medium\",\n    86\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 8000\n    87\t  },\n    88\t  \"idea\": {\n    89\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    90\t    \"prompt_version\": \"idea-v11\",\n    91\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"none\",\n    92\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n    93\t  },\n    94\t  \"collision\": {\n    95\t    \"model\": \"gpt-6-luna\",\n    96\t    \"prompt_version\": \"collision-v2\",\n    97\t    \"reasoning_effort\": \"low\",\n    98\t    \"max_output_tokens\": 4000\n    99\t  }\n   100\t}\n     1\t# Linking related questions: the build design, version 5 (D694, D695; for council review before code)\n     2\t\n     3\tAlex chose A (D694) and narrowed the first version (D695, \"只连数字题\"): a link joins a **newly opened number question** and an **open\n     4\tnumber question it was shown**, in either reading direction; both are asset questions with five-rung ladders and typed bounds. No\n     5\ttheme, event or same-article pair is linked in this version. A chosen link leaves filing alone (D694 (a)). Version 1 of this document\n     6\twas reviewed in council R round 4 (`codex-r4.md`, NOT READY), version 2 in round 5 (`codex-r5.md`, NOT READY), version 3 in round 6\n     7\t(`codex-r6.md`, NOT READY), version 4 in round 7 (`codex-r7.md`, NOT READY); each finding is answered below (§10).\n     8\t\n     9\t## 0. Versions and entry points\n    10\t\n    11\t- `poc/config/poc-v119.json`: poc-v118 with `matching.engine` `jev-links` and `rejudging.prompt_version` `judging-v8`; nothing else.\n    12\t- `poc/config/poc-v120.json` (D705): poc-v119 with `matching.link_questions` `links-v2`, version 2 of the READS and SIGN texts\n    13\t  (`docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md` §5); poc-v119 reads `links-v1` by default and is unchanged.\n    14\t- `judging-v8.txt` is a byte copy of `judging-v7.txt`; only the code-built dependency block differs (§3). A request with no dependency is\n    15\t  byte-equal under v7 and v8.\n    16\t- `config.ENGINES` gains `jev-links`. Every place that tests `engine == 'jev'` (`round._match`, `scripts/replay.py`,\n    17\t  `parallel_day.ParallelDay`, `budget_replay.py` defaults) treats `jev-links` as Jev; only `round.run` asks the link questions, and only\n    18\t  under `jev-links`. Existing Jev requests are unchanged (`jev.request_for` holds model, state and questions only).\n    19\t- **Who may run poc-v119 (an enforced boundary):** only the July harness (`TEST-PLAN.md`). `scripts/replay.py` and\n    20\t  `budget_replay.py` refuse a configuration whose matching engine is `jev-links` (\"not a product entry point in this version\"). The\n    21\t  harness holds `live_lock.acquire` on each sequence's store for the whole run, refuses a store whose last day is unfinished, and never\n    22\t  resumes a sequence that stopped: a stopped sequence is final and reported as stopped. Each harness ledger is **marked harness-only**\n    23\t  before the run (a table `harness_only` holding the harness's name and the date), and both ordinary writers refuse it under any\n    24\t  configuration before routing an item (`scripts/replay.py`'s `refuse_harness_ledger`, called beside `refuse_seeded_ledger`, which\n    25\t  `budget_replay.py` already calls); read-only inspection stays open. So the serial path's unchecked restarts (a\n    26\t  sequence reused under another configuration or input, a second writer) cannot reach a v119 store. Making poc-v119 runnable from the\n    27\t  product entry point is a later decision, with its own restart rules.\n    28\t- **A store written by poc-v119 opened by poc-v118:** allowed; v118 writes no link, renders a stored link with today's v7 line, and\n    29\t  filing skips it (filing reads the stored kind, not the configuration). A run is meant to keep one configuration; this is the defined\n    30\t  outcome if it does not.\n    31\t- Pins (`tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py`): the v7 pins stay; added: `judging-v8.txt`'s sha (equal to v7's), the two new\n    32\t  question builders' output, judging-v8's schema (equal to v7's), and a request-level control: one ledger with a link rendered under v8\n    33\t  (exact text) and under v7 (today's text), and one without a link, byte-equal under both.\n    34\t\n    35\t## 1. Where selection runs: after matching has settled what opens\n    36\t\n    37\tIn `round.run`, under `jev-links` only, a new step **after the evidence-only second matching call returns and before the `matched`\n    38\tsuccess marker**, on the first call's `checked.outcomes` and lists:\n    39\t1. From `checked.outcomes` take the candidates whose outcome is `new` or `succession`; `identity.batch_plan(handover.candidates,\n    40\t   checked.outcomes)` gives their aliases; one canonical candidate per stored question. A candidate refused or not opened is not asked.\n    41\t2. **Eligible pairs:** the canonical candidate C and each open thesis T on C's list (its search list plus the item's shown questions,\n    42\t   `lists.candidate_lists[C] + shown`, the list its relation questions used), when both are **number questions**: asset kind; a\n    43\t   measure outside `identity.EVENT_MEASURES` (C's own key, T's stored key); five rungs whose canonical labels run Strongly bullish to\n    44\t   Strongly bearish or the reverse; a **typed direction** (§5). C's rungs are taken as the writer will store them\n    45\t   (`writing.oriented_like` for a succession, which may reverse the whole ladder with its labels). A pair outside this set is not\n    46\t   asked. Same-article pairs are not asked (D695).\n    47\t3. **Stage 1, one Jev job per C:** state = `candidate_state(C)`; per eligible T the `READS` question (§2) with `thesis_text(T)`.\n    48\t4. **Stage 2, one Jev job per C with a passing stage-1 answer:** the shared state stays `candidate_state(C)`; per such pair one of two\nWORDING-V2.md:67:## 5. The product version (D705: version 2 as a separately versioned, reviewed configuration)\nWORDING-V2.md:83:| Prior decisions | D359 (a configuration naming a version the code does not build is refused), D694 §0 (entry points), D695, D703, D705. |\n../../../docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10583:## D705 · 2026-11-21 · The version-2 link question passes its registered gate; council R: version 2 goes to the paid design\n../../research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/mutants.log\n../../research/2026-11-21-whole-window/mutants.log\n../../research/2026-11-21-whole-window/v120-replay-3.log\n../../research/2026-11-21-whole-window/v120-replay-2.log\n../../research/2026-11-21-whole-window/v120-replay-1.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
