{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** `poc-v120` reproduces the measured requests exactly. The blocker is in config validation: the loader accepts values and placements that the matching-only contract says to refuse. [Version contract](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/WORDING-V2.md:67) · [Config loader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:80)\n\n- **Blocking — validate presence, section, and value.** I reproduced three accepted configs: `matching.link_questions: null` under `jev`, the same explicit `null` under `jev-links` silently selecting V1, and `rejudging` with `engine: jev-links` and `link_questions: links-v2`. `_setting` treats `null` as omission and checks the engine without checking the section. Default to V1 only when the key is absent from `matching` under `jev-links`. When the key is present, require that section and engine and one of the two exact strings. Add loader tests for the three reproduced cases. [Loader](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/config.py:89) · [Existing rejection tests](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_links.py:374)\n- **Request isolation holds for the named configs.** I verified the v118 and v119 checksums and confirmed that v120’s only settings change is `matching.link_questions`. READS, SIGN, and cycle corrections all receive the configured version. I compared all **51** replayed request and response strings against the three probe archives. They matched exactly, including the missing full stop. The ordinary launchers still refuse both linking versions. [v120 config](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/config/poc-v120.json:68) · [READS](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:262) · [SIGN](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:287) · [Correction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:310) · [Replay check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:409) · [Launcher guard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/scripts/replay.py:66)\n- **The tests are decisive for the six new mutants.** I reran the focused tests and those six mutants in memory. Each failed at the intended criteria assertion, config refusal, or V2 pin. The earlier seven control/mutant pairs are recorded in the supplied log. The rejection tests cover the named bad version and wrong engine, leaving the three loader cases above uncovered. [Stage assertions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_links.py:385) · [Frozen pin](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_frozen_questions_and_judgement.py:43) · [Mutation log](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/mutants.log:1)\n- **Two additional isolation notes.** The value table misses an indirect reader: `parallel_day.environment_key` serializes the full config, so adding the field changes v118’s manifest fingerprint despite its unchanged checksum. Runtime changes already trigger that manifest’s refusal, so record this reader without weakening the guard. Separately, the historical probe helper reassigns `READS` and `SIGN`, while the builders now read the original dictionaries through `QUESTION_SETS`. I verified that the helper still builds V1 and is refused at the probe transport boundary. Restore that helper or mark the historical entry points retired and point readers to `v120-replay`. Neither issue changes the 51-request replay result. [Manifest fingerprint](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/parallel_day.py:34) · [Manifest guard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/parallel_day.py:68) · [Historical probe helper](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/window_test.py:327) · [Versioned builders](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/links.py:64)"}}
